{
  "challenge_id": "lc_3905",
  "measurement_note": "Size is V = n * m, the number of grid cells. A checkerboard supplies V/2 distinct sources and leaves every other cell to resolve simultaneous neighboring offers. Layered multi-source BFS processes O(V) cells and edges, while the slower control compares every cell with every source in O(V * |sources|) = O(V^2) time. The 4x tier steps keep that correct slower control below the execution safety cap so scaling, rather than termination, decides its verdict.",
